window.docContents[66].resolve({"/rules/RG1007/#RG1007-configuration":{"contents":"No source option, attribute or command-line flag makes this rule pass on a claimed surface. set_option linter.regula false and regula.localFoundation never waive it: lake lint, the build-lint policy target and axiomGate still apply the rule. Where Regula's local linter reports a finding during a project build (axiomGate and the policy target keep it on by default; lake lint builds with it off, whatever the source sets linter.regula to), that finding is a build warning, so the result is INCOMPLETE under RG2003 instead of carrying this rule's finding. Switching the local linter off changes which finding is reported, never whether the result is accepted. Hiding the diagnostic does not establish the property it checks.\n\nProject enforcement runs through lake lint (incremental), lake lint -- --fresh and lake exe axiomGate (fresh whole-project audits from empty build output), and the build-lint policy target. See the adoption guide.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG1007: Executable contracts require supported closed evidence","header":"Configuration and exceptions","id":"/rules/RG1007/#RG1007-configuration"},"/rules/RG4004/#RG4004-configuration":{"contents":"There is no name-based allowlist for native proofs; authentication is required for every teaching fence.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG4004: Teaching examples require authenticated compiler classification","header":"Configuration and exceptions","id":"/rules/RG4004/#RG4004-configuration"},"/rules/RG5003/#RG5003-configuration":{"contents":"No source option or command-line flag makes this rule pass on a claimed surface. set_option linter.regula false and regula.localFoundation never waive it: lake lint, the build-lint policy target and axiomGate still apply the rule. Where Regula's local linter reports a finding during a project build (axiomGate and the policy target keep it on by default; lake lint builds with it off, whatever the source sets linter.regula to), that finding is a build warning, so the result is INCOMPLETE under RG2003 instead of carrying this rule's finding. Switching the local linter off changes which finding is reported, never whether the result is accepted. Hiding the diagnostic does not establish the property it checks.\n\nThe rule checks only declarations registered with @[regula_material] from Regula.MaterialClaim. Removing a registration from a material declaration changes the reviewed claim, not only this rule's result.\n\nProject enforcement runs through lake lint (incremental), lake lint -- --fresh and lake exe axiomGate (fresh whole-project audits from empty build output), and the build-lint policy target. See the adoption guide.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG5003: Registered public material declarations require an Intent section","header":"Configuration and exceptions","id":"/rules/RG5003/#RG5003-configuration"},"/versions/#versions-routes":{"contents":"* https://rbeauchamp.github.io/regula/dev/rules/<ID>/ is the development explanation. It always shows the most recent successfully deployed revision of main; the linter's diagnostics link here.* https://rbeauchamp.github.io/regula/rev/<commit>/rules/<ID>/ is the snapshot of one published commit. Each deployment publishes the snapshot of its own commit and every earlier published snapshot, byte for byte: a snapshot is archived before it is deployed, the archive is append-only, and a deployment must contain every archived snapshot.* https://rbeauchamp.github.io/regula/v/<version>/rules/<ID>/ is reserved for immutable pages of released packages. No package has been released, so no such page exists.\n\nA route that is not published shows the site's not-available page, which names the source of every revision on GitHub. It never redirects to the latest rules: an old link cannot silently acquire changed semantics. Rule IDs are never reused for a changed rule; a retired rule keeps a page that says so.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Versions and evidence","header":"Routes","id":"/versions/#versions-routes"}});